From: libpldm portable build maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] environ: Preserve wire layout on Darwin and MinGW

Developed against upstream be4f63e36408921e76d868593176377de84e945e.

Use Apple's byte-order primitives and compiler byte swaps on little-endian
MinGW. Route endian users through the existing public byteorder header,
install its companion header, and propagate MinGW's required GNU bitfield
layout to pkg-config consumers. Keep a bounded memmem fallback for Windows.

The deprecated linker alias list is currently empty. Fail explicitly if
upstream adds an alias instead of passing ELF-only --defsym to Mach-O/PE
linkers or silently losing an old entry point in a static archive.
